WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.415
An agent trace should connect the user request, model calls, tool calls,

00:00:05.415 --> 00:00:07.671
validation decisions, and final outcome.

00:00:07.821 --> 00:00:14.441
Record model and prompt versions, durations, error categories, token usage, and source

00:00:14.441 --> 00:00:14.992
identifiers.

00:00:15.142 --> 00:00:18.587
Avoid logging raw secrets or unnecessary customer data.

00:00:18.737 --> 00:00:22.774
Debugging should answer which step failed and what authority it had, not

00:00:22.774 --> 00:00:24.456
merely display a large transcript.

00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:29.095
Deploy behind authentication, ingress limits, and controlled egress.

00:00:29.245 --> 00:00:33.730
Separate readiness from liveness and ensure shutdown drains or records in-flight work.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:39.627
Track business success, unsupported-answer rate, and cost alongside HTTP latency.

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:44.363
Roll out model or prompt changes gradually and retain a rollback path

00:00:44.363 --> 00:00:45.891
with comparable evaluation results.

00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:51.258
A support request may return HTTP 200 while giving an unsupported delivery

00:00:51.258 --> 00:00:51.693
promise.

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:54.616
Therefore transport success alone is insufficient.

00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:59.521
The lab’s trace contains synthetic data for inspection; a production trace needs

00:00:59.521 --> 00:01:01.106
access controls and redaction.

00:01:01.256 --> 00:01:06.630
The application should retain exact effect IDs while minimizing sensitive narrative content.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.853
Design a dashboard and three alerts for the support assistant.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:16.569
Create a deployment checklist including model rollout, evaluation gates, rollback, retention, and

00:01:16.569 --> 00:01:18.210
emergency tool disablement.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:23.652
Alert on a sustained increase in failed tasks or unsupported claims, exhausted

00:01:23.652 --> 00:01:25.857
provider quota, and authorization violations.

00:01:26.007 --> 00:01:28.908
Choose thresholds from a baseline and business impact.

00:01:29.058 --> 00:01:33.570
Tool disablement should stop risky effects without requiring every prompt to be

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:33.946
rewritten.

00:01:34.096 --> 00:01:34.767
Question.

00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.847
What makes an AI trace useful?

00:01:36.997 --> 00:01:37.574
Answer.

00:01:37.724 --> 00:01:43.229
It connects a specific outcome to versioned inputs, decisions, evidence, and dependency

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:45.523
timings while protecting sensitive data.

00:01:45.673 --> 00:01:46.344
Question.

00:01:46.494 --> 00:01:49.004
Why can a prompt-only release need rollback?

00:01:49.154 --> 00:01:49.731
Answer.

00:01:49.881 --> 00:01:55.129
It can alter tool selection, answer quality, token usage, latency, and failure

00:01:55.129 --> 00:01:58.191
behavior even when Java code is unchanged.
